==Trivia==
*Puffzerker's Japanese name, Teppō (テッポー), is derived from 鉄砲 ''teppō'', which not only means "gun", but is also a [[wikipedia:Kansai dialect|Kansai]] slang term for pufferfish; and 鉄砲玉 ''teppōdama'', which literally translates to "gun ball" and means a bullet, gunshot, or a person who goes out and never returns, and by extension, someone who plays such a role, especially an assassin or hitman. In [[wikipedia:Yakuza#Structure|yakuza groups]], the ''oyabun'' (boss) expects all ''kobun'' (subordinates) to be ''teppōdama'' for their boss; mere bullets to be fired and sacrifice themselves when needed. Since Puffzerker is an aquatic animal with high speed, the name may also involve 鉄砲水 ''teppōmizu'' (flash flood).
*Puffzerker's [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] trait may be a reference to the [[wikipedia:Redline pufferfish|redline pufferfish]].
*Much like [[Super Metal Hippoe]], [[Angel Fanboy]] and many [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] and [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] enemies before them, Puffzerker and [[Commander Ostromeda]] were technically event enemies for a short time, until their proper introduction to [[Zero Legends]] in [[Version 14.5 Update|Version 14.5]].
**Both Puffzerker and Commander Ostromeda debuted in the [[Anniversary/12 1/2 Year|12th and 1/2 Anniversary]], making them the only enemies from anniversary events to have descriptions.
**Since the 12th and 1/2 Anniversary still hadn't been released outside of Japan by the time [[A Journey of Moments]] was added to other versions, Puffzerker's first appearance in all versions except [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]] was [[Tower of the Time Lord]].

